            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "user_channel/user_mgmt.cpp",
                    "line": 822,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "When creating a new user, the default role is USER \u2014 does this need to be synchronized?\n\nAlso, I saw an earlier mailing list post describing the mapping between user roles and user groups.\nhttps://lists.ozlabs.org/pipermail/openbmc/2020-November/024061.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\nBut I\u2019m not sure whether there\u2019s a new specification for the role-to-group relationship?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "user_channel/user_mgmt.cpp",
                    "line": 822,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hieu Huynh",
                        "email": "hieuh@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "hieuhuynh-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi George,\n\n> When creating a new user, the default role is USER \u2014 does this need to be synchronized?\n\nI don't believe this needs to be updated because we already have the set privileges command.\n\n> But I\u2019m not sure whether there\u2019s a new specification for the role-to-group relationship?\n\nCurrently, there is no specification defining the mapping between the group and Privilege Role. As shown in https://github.com/openbmc/meta-phosphor/blob/master/recipes-core/dropbear/dropbear/dropbear.default, if an accounts does not include the priv-admin group in its group list, the user will be an able to SSH into the BMC due to Dropbear's enforced restriction."
                }
            ],
